{"skill":{"slug":"hubspot","displayName":"HubSpot"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1771272245454,"changelog":"Fix security flags: added homepage for provenance, declared curl/jq as required binaries, updated metadata format","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":8374,"sha256":"8222c27c3906b42eaeb93ab9935192c01fba9c0f97216055578773c060529056","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_meta.json","size":126,"sha256":"f92b7efb5a21bb3209277aae00687f3b48dd659e064efc8e49afc38f80f8d424","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1853,"sha256":"d3dd0b6335947432f18c4afce28b33f0c580ef1f65d5c23c1110e8136bf9c0d0","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789016853226,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"0219f0d167e7a747984103b5d9c34fa8478c4894dfcb976a099cd0c01664b15b","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/0219f0d167e7a747984103b5d9c34fa8478c4894dfcb976a099cd0c01664b15b","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: hubspot\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill bundle provides a legitimate integration with the HubSpot CRM and CMS API. All `curl` commands target the official `https://api.hubapi.com` domain and use the `HUBSPOT_ACCESS_TOKEN` as expected for authentication. There is no evidence of data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, malicious command execution, persistence mechanisms, obfuscation, or prompt injection attempts against the agent to subvert its intended behavior. The use of `curl` and `jq` is standard for API interaction, and while placeholders like `{contactId}` could present a shell injection vulnerability if the agent's execution environment does not properly sanitize user input, this is a platform-level vulnerability rather than malicious intent within the skill's content itself.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159831056},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":48,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":41,"checkedAt":1789016853226},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill is a straightforward HubSpot API helper, but it gives raw commands that can read and change CRM/CMS data using a private app token without enough safety guidance.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Using curl, jq, network access to api.hubapi.com, and HUBSPOT_ACCESS_TOKEN is proportionate for a HubSpot API skill, but the token may carry broad CRM/CMS permissions depending on how the user scopes it.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No installer, dependency download, executable script, or remote payload retrieval is present. The skill is a Markdown instruction file requiring curl, jq, and a HubSpot token.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions include POST and PATCH examples for creating contacts and deals, updating contact properties, assigning owners, and creating associations, but do not clearly warn that these change live HubSpot data or require explicit confirmation before mutation.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No system persistence or local privilege escalation is present, but the skill relies on a high-value HubSpot private app access token and gives only a bare environment-variable example without secret handling, least-privilege, rotation, or logging cautions.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The declared purpose is HubSpot CRM and CMS integration, and the commands target HubSpot API endpoints for contacts, companies, deals, owners, associations, CMS pages, domains, and files. Those capabilities fit the purpose, but include sensitive CRM data access and live mutations.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this before installing if the agent may operate against a production HubSpot portal. Use a minimally scoped private app token, keep it out of files and shared logs, prefer a test portal for examples, and require explicit approval before running POST or PATCH commands that create or modify CRM records.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The HubSpot private app token is expected for direct HubSpot API calls, but the artifact lacks adequate credential-safety guidance for a token that may expose customer and business data.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The scanner concern about missing credential-handling guidance is supported by the artifact: setup only shows HUBSPOT_ACCESS_TOKEN=pat-na2-xxxxx and repeated Authorization headers.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The concern about live mutating examples is supported: the skill includes create, update, assign-owner, and association-create commands without sandbox or confirmation guidance.\n[E1] expected: The external transmissions are to HubSpot API endpoints and are coherent with the stated integration purpose; I did not find evidence of unrelated telemetry or exfiltration destinations.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789016853226}}}}}